  "reference_no_of_permission_being_relied_on": "Full Planning Permission (ref:19/01872/FULL as amended by 19/05426/NMA) and Listed Building Consent (ref:19/01873/LBC as amended by 19/05385/LBC) were approved on 6th August 2019 and 23rd August 2019 respectively, for the below descriptions of development:\n\n19/01872/FULL as amended by 19/05426/NMA: “Amendments to planning permission dated 4 June 2019 (RN: 19/01872) for: Alterations and extensions to the buildings in connection with their use as a private members' club (sui generis) and a cafe (Class A3), works involve the partial demolition and rebuild of the Halkin Street mews facade, replacement Headfort Place mews facade and new mews roof mansard, erection of a single storey extension to the rear of the main building at the second floor level, the installation of external terraces at third and fifth floors, roof plant enclosures, openings to light well elevations, new metal railing behind lowered parapet and to the new terrace over the new extension, alteration of vaults and associated works. Namely, to allow amendments to the decision notice to include a number of design conditions and amendments to others.\"\n\n19/01873/LBC as amended by 19/05385/LBC: “Amendments to listed building consent dated 04 June 2019 (RN: 19/01873/LBC) for the: Alterations and extensions to the buildings, works involve the partial demolition and rebuild of the Halkin Street mews facade, replacement Headfort Place mews facade and new mews roof mansard, erection of a single storey extension to the rear of the main building at the second floor level, the installation of external terraces at third and fifth floors, roof plant enclosures, openings to light well elevations, new metal railing behind lowered parapet and to the new terrace over the new extension alteration of vaults, extensive internal alterations and other associated works. Namely, to amend the decision notice to include design conditions.”\n",
